1
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,600
Who would believe a small investment

2
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:38,480
<i>gives huge returns? Totally crazy.</i>

3
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,680
I'll quickly find
some bigger investors for you.

4
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,520
If you can't help me,

5
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:47,000
just stay out of it.
I'll handle it myself.

6
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,720
Work is work, personal life is personal.

7
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,520
<i>I will be totally fine</i>

8
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,560
<i>if you make Mam</i>
<i>fall head over heels for you.</i>

9
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:58,080
I haven't been this happy in a long time.

10
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:00,560
<i>Looks like our Ms. Mam</i>

11
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:03,360
is totally falling for Mr. Anderson.

12
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:05,440
Will someone please tell me
what's going on?

13
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,800
Get rid of him.

14
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:12,560
I think we still have a chance.
We should wait a little longer.

15
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,120
I hate waiting.

16
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,120
I hate losing to Mam!

17
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,800
MARK, PETER, PEAK 2

18
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,360
Hey, can someone answer the phone?

19
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,680
It's driving me crazy!

20
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,280
PEAK 1

21
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,840
Who's calling Mr. Peak's number?

22
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,120
Hello.

23
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:53,400
Hello, Peter.

24
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,600
<i>How are you, Mr. Peak?</i>

25
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:01,440
<i>Have you talked to your father</i>
<i>about investing in M Power yet?</i>

26
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,520
That's great.

27
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,240
If Miss Mam knew, she'd be so happy.

28
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,360
In that case,

29
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,200
would next week work?

30
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,320
Our company is holding a seminar.

31
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:21,000
I'd like to take the opportunity
to invite you and your father

32
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:23,040
to sign the contract together that day.

33
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,400
Perfect, Mr. Peak.

34
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:28,640
See you then.

35
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,960
Mr. Peak's father is interested
in making a major investment with us.

36
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,920
Done. I told you there's still a chance.

37
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,640
Who would've thought

38
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:49,640
they'd come back
to swallow up their old target?

39
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,760
That's because they're greedy.

40
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,280
I'm loving this!

41
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,640
So, who's Peak's dad?

42
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,560
Yeah.

43
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,920
Wait, don't tell me

44
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,080
you're actually bringing
your real dad into the mission?

45
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,800
No way. It has to be someone on our team.

46
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,520
Then who could it be?
They've already seen all of us.

47
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:22,200
What's this? Still so serious, huh?

48
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,160
I told you, every problem has a solution.

49
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:29,120
Once we know the cause, we handle it.
That's it. It's over.

50
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,880
We'll deal with it tomorrow.

51
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:40,880
What? Why are you all staring at me?

52
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,520
Please register here.

53
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,840
Hello, View!

54
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,320
You can handle this solo, right?

55
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,160
I have to.

56
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:36,120
Yeah. We can't mess this up again.

57
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,360
Hello, Peak.

58
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:53,480
-Hello, Mam.
-Hello, sir.

59
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,880
Thank you so much
for bringing him here today.

60
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,040
My pleasure.

61
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,760
Peak, my precious son,

62
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:04,360
has told me so much about you.

63
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,720
About how your company is on the rise.

64
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:10,680
If I don't invest now, I'll miss the boat.

65
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:16,520
I got it all right, didn't I, son?

66
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,880
Yes, Dad.

67
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,240
No wonder he's a rising star
in the startup world.

68
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,440
He has excellent judgment.

69
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,960
But I have one important question

70
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,560
for you, Miss Mam.

71
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,000
If I invest 50 million,

72
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,840
would that be okay?

73
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,680
That would be wonderful.

74
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,600
How about

75
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,480
after I finish my presentation,

76
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:48,240
we talk about signing the contract?

77
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:52,120
Perfect. Just saying it out loud
makes me feel better.

78
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,400
Thank you.

79
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,760
The team is here to get me.

80
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:03,200
I'll leave Peak and his father
in your care.

81
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,480
Of course, Ms. Mam.

82
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,520
Excuse me for now.

83
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,360
Yes, thank you.

84
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,320
Please, go ahead.

85
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:10,920
Sure.

86
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,880
-Yes.
-Ahem.

87
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,080
Dad, can we go now?

88
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,720
Got it! Got it!

89
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,240
This way, please.

90
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:40,360
-Sure.
-Let's go, Dad.

91
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,520
Hey, wait.

92
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,680
Yes, sir.

93
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:00,720
What are you doing here?

94
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,720
I'm here to fix the lights.

95
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,760
Do you know where the control room is?

96
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,240
The lights? Nobody reported any problems.

97
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,480
Sir.

98
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,520
Everything's fine for now.

99
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,560
But in a moment, there'll be a problem.

100
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,000
-Right this way.
-Thank you.

101
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,120
-Dad.
-Yeah?

102
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:30,000
I want to use the restroom.

103
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:34,200
Again? You already stopped
at a few on the way here.

104
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,039
Here's what we'll do.
After I sign the contract,

105
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,480
we'll have the doctor
check you thoroughly.

106
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:42,760
My son, Peak,

107
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,120
has a bit of a bladder problem.

108
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,520
Dad, you don't have to tell everyone.
I'm embarrassed.

109
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,200
No problem.

110
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,840
The restroom is through
this door, on the right.

111
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,280
-On the right?
-Yes.

112
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,560
-Thank you.
-Go ahead. Hurry up!

113
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,000
Whether he's sitting or standing,
he wets himself.

114
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,200
After you.

115
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,760
He probably got it from his mom.

116
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,880
I'm taking the elevator
up to Mam's office floor.

117
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,840
STAND WITHIN THE DESIGNATED AREA
NO TALKING

118
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,720
Mung! Hey, stop!

119
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,440
Okay, it's clear. Go!

120
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,840
VERIFIED! YOLLADA ARAYASAI
BOARD OF DIRECTORS

121
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,520
Five more minutes, Ms. Mam.

122
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,480
Got it.

123
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,200
PETER

124
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,600
The card, huh?

125
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,640
I'll go check the office.

126
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,080
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

127
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,640
I just need a moment.

128
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:01,680
Sure, take your time.
I can manage on my own.

129
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:11,000
Hurry.

130
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:13,720
I think he's starting to catch on.

131
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,520
Okay, Uncle. That's enough for now.

132
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,920
Angpao, check where Peter is.

133
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,080
Okay, one sec.

134
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,440
Everyone on the 23rd floor,

135
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:27,080
go check Ms. Mam's office immediately.

136
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:32,000
There. Found him.

137
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,680
Mungkorn, he's taking the elevator up.

138
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,080
Hurry and get into Mam's office.

139
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:45,200
Go check Ms. Mam's office too.

140
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,880
Nothing unusual in her office.

141
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,600
Hold on. I'm coming in.

142
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,400
Okay, the computer's on, Pao.

143
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,760
Wait for it to boot up,
then plug in the flash drive.

144
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,520
Hello, everyone.

145
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:42,560
<i>First, I'd like to sincerely</i>
<i>thank all of you</i>

146
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:46,200
<i>for trusting and always</i>
<i>supporting M Power.</i>

147
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,080
The show's started.
Who's bothering us now?

148
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,600
-Go check.
-Yes.

149
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,560
Wow, so this is the control room.
I've been looking for it.

150
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:04,400
Is there a problem?

151
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,640
Okay, the flash drive's in.

152
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,480
-Can you do it?
-If I can't,

153
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,320
no one in the world can.

154
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,720
It's connected, Mungkorn. Get out now.

155
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:44,680
How's it going?

156
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,800
I don't see anything here.

157
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:05,440
The future is ours to choose.

158
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:08,560
Here's an important opportunity
for everyone

159
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:13,520
because I'm raising the return from 10%

160
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,240
to 15%!

161
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,960
Almost. Come on, kid.

162
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,720
Didn't make it?

163
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,800
Data's loaded!

164
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:11,800
We've got all the names and accounts
in the entire M Power network.

165
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,240
Chen, any problems in the control room?

166
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,600
No problems here.

167
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,400
-Go ahead with the next step.
-Okay.

168
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:25,960
Click.

169
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:30,760
Wait. Where's Mung?

170
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,560
Mungkorn, are you out yet?

171
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,600
Nowhere else but M Power

172
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,320
can offer everyone this much.

173
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:11,960
We're all going to get rich together!

174
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:12,960
-Rich!
-Rich!

175
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:16,040
Rich! Rich! Rich!

176
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,440
Can we say it again?

177
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,920
Rich! Rich! Rich!

178
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:12,319
<i>Mr. Peter, there's a problem on stage.</i>

179
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,599
<i>The stage video has been hacked.</i>

180
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,359
Hurry to the control room! Now!

181
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,240
To the control room, move!

182
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:39,560
<i>You run a pyramid scheme company,</i>
<i>don't you?</i>

183
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,480
<i>No, I don't.</i>

184
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,480
Wait, what?

185
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,840
A pyramid scheme?

186
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:49,640
No, I don't. I really don't.

187
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:52,200
Honestly, I've never done
anything like that.

188
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,560
<i>If you don't tell me what's going on,</i>

189
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:57,600
<i>I won't be able to help you, honey.</i>

190
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,600
<i>Yes.</i>

191
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,160
<i>It's all true.</i>

192
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:14,320
<i>But I've been trying to shut it down,</i>

193
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,720
<i>so we could run away and be together.</i>

194
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,800
What did she just say?

195
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,520
Get something to cut the chain!

196
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:42,960
-Now!
-Go!

197
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,760
Ms. Mam.

198
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,520
How could you do this?

199
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,880
This is a scam!

200
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:56,480
Give us our money back!

201
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,240
-Yeah!
-Give our money back!

202
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,560
This is a scam!

203
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,440
Why are you like this?

204
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:03,040
Give us our money back!

205
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,040
Yeah! Get out!

206
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:06,640
Give us our money back!

207
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:10,520
-Give it back!
-Get out!

208
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,560
How could you do this?

209
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,200
Why are you like this?

210
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,760
Stop!

211
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:21,440
Stop! Don't do it!

212
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:23,440
Don't!

213
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:26,200
Stop!

214
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,560
Ms. Mam!

215
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,000
Ms. Mam! Quick, get backstage!

216
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:32,760
Give us our money back!

217
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,080
Ms. Mam, hurry!

218
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,440
Peter, I just saw Phayak.

219
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,120
I really saw him.

220
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:48,560
We've been outsmarted by Hong.

221
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,600
That's impossible. I saw him
get shot dead with my own eyes.

222
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,520
But I really saw him.

223
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,880
Right there, in the crowd.

224
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,200
Go help up front!

225
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,240
Excuse us!

226
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:05,800
Hey, you! Take Ms. Mam
out the back, quickly!

227
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,520
-But…
-Ms. Mam, go now.

228
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:10,000
I'll handle the situation here.

229
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:10,920
Go ahead.

230
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,240
Take care of her.

231
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,280
Yes.

232
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:20,160
Give me back my money!

233
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,600
Give me back my money!

234
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:25,920
-Everyone!
-Give me back my money!

235
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,760
Please calm down.
This is all a misunderstanding.

236
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:30,120
What misunderstanding?

237
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:32,880
Right, everyone? What about our money?

238
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:35,280
-Yeah!
-Give me back my money!

239
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:36,440
This way, Ms. Mam.

240
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,520
Wait a moment.

241
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,160
Why stop? Why aren't we moving?

242
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,880
Someone wants to see you, Ms. Mam.

243
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:48,240
Who?

244
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:55,240
The one you once betrayed.

245
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:12,280
You! You're on Hong's side?

246
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:14,200
We're all on the same side.

247
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:30,520
You tricked her perfectly, son.

248
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:33,840
You!

249
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,680
This isn't what everyone thinks.

250
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:40,160
Give me back my money!

251
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:42,320
Calm down. It's
a misunderstanding, everyone.

252
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:47,400
<i>On behalf of Admin,</i>

253
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,880
<i>I have taken control of all the financial</i>

254
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:54,320
<i>and account systems of M Power.</i>

255
00:21:56,760 --> 00:22:00,640
<i>And I am now returning the money</i>
<i>that was stolen</i>

256
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:05,320
<i>to the accounts of every victim.</i>

257
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,280
What? Really?

258
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:10,400
Will we get our money back?

259
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:13,080
No way.

260
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:15,480
There's no way
you could access my accounts.

261
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,760
Why not?

262
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:21,000
Mr. Anderson

263
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:23,920
knows every password to your accounts.

264
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:41,200
The passcode is 1782.

265
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:45,160
This is bad.

266
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,120
-Check it immediately! Check the phone!
-Check…

267
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,200
Check the money!

268
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,440
Screen passcode, 1782.

269
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:57,280
Bank passcode,

270
00:22:58,080 --> 00:23:01,200
<i>010782.</i>

271
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,880
Done.

272
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:14,160
Done, Pao. Access granted.

273
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:16,240
Account number,

274
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:19,840
<i>412-644-23-8,</i>

275
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:21,800
Yollada Arayasai.

276
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:26,840
Passcode, 010782.

277
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:31,400
Okay, ready, transfer!

278
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:40,080
The money really came in, everyone!

279
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,160
-It's true!
-The money's in!

280
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:48,880
Thank you, everyone!

281
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:51,800
-I don't know.
-Some stranger helped us.

282
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,200
The transfers are all complete.

283
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,560
NO ENTRY

284
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,320
Hey!

285
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,520
You surprised to see me?

286
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:11,400
You!

287
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:13,400
You were supposed to be dead.

288
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:16,000
Then who's standing here?

289
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:17,480
A ghost?

290
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,760
You really thought I was dead?

291
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:46,200
Bro!

292
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,320
Bro, wake up!

293
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,040
He left.

294
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:56,560
What if the bullet had actually hit me?

295
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,880
Don't worry about that.

296
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:01,440
When I shot you,
it hit the armor right here anyway.

297
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,840
But I was scared out of my mind.

298
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:07,720
If Peter had hit me in the head,
I'd be toast by now.

299
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:09,720
That hurts so much.

300
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:10,720
Let's see.

301
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:17,040
Direct hit.

302
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,360
I told you to wear it, bro.

303
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:21,080
Better safe than sorry.

304
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,400
You!

305
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:30,120
And making you break your finger
to get out of the warehouse,

306
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:32,240
you really think we didn't plan that?

307
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:34,440
Why did you do all this?

308
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:37,160
To make you spill the entire plan to Mam.

309
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:39,120
So today's event could happen.

310
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:43,080
Otherwise, I wouldn't have had the chance
to expose you in front of everyone.

311
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:47,800
You bastard!

312
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:57,640
Haven't you learned anything?

313
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:00,000
When you mess with us,

314
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:03,200
you've got to think of everything.

315
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:25,720
Peter's out cold now.

316
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:35,040
You wretch!

317
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:39,240
But not as bad as what you did to me, Mam!

318
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,720
Consider it karma

319
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:46,160
for betraying us
back in the Kamnan Chang incident.

320
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,600
Then you all have to pay too.

321
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:57,760
You took ten million of my money,
didn't you?

322
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,280
Wait.

323
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:05,160
What ten million? When we split it,

324
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:06,720
each of us got only
a few hundred thousand.

325
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:09,920
Yeah, just a few hundred thousand.

326
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:19,360
So that's how it is.

327
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:21,360
Hong.

328
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,720
You kept all the money
for yourself, didn't you?

329
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:29,600
What are you guys talking about?

330
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:32,720
Ask Hong where she stashed the money.

331
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:38,680
When the money was moved,
one of my bags went missing.

332
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:46,760
Who else could've taken it if not Hong?

333
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:47,800
Stop lying already!

334
00:27:47,880 --> 00:27:49,360
You're the liar!

335
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:53,720
For the past 13 years,
while you were running in panic,

336
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:57,720
you didn't even know
Hong spent all the money herself.

337
00:28:01,080 --> 00:28:02,520
You idiots.

338
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:12,000
What are they doing?
Why aren't they coming down yet?

339
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,880
Ris, the police are here.

340
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:30,000
Tell the others upstairs.

341
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:35,720
Chen, Mungkorn, what are you doing?
The police are here.

342
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:38,800
-Hey, Koh. Move, the police are here.
-Yeah.

343
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:47,480
Sis, can we deal
with the other stuff later?

344
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:49,280
The police are here.
Let's get out of here.

345
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:52,120
You fools!

346
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:53,680
You've been tricked by Hong!

347
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:56,360
You idiots! She totally fooled you!

348
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:58,640
-Let's go.
-Curse yourself!

349
00:28:58,720 --> 00:28:59,880
-Come on, sis.
-No, you!

350
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:00,880
-Hong!
-Bro, let's go.

351
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:01,800
-You fools!
-You're done!

352
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:03,920
-Give me back my money! Let me go!
-Let's go! Move now!

353
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:06,400
-You idiots! You fools!
-Let's get out of here!

354
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:09,680
You've been tricked, idiots!

355
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:16,120
Get back here, you bastards!

356
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:17,960
Let me go!

357
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:18,920
M POWER LEADERS ARRESTED
OVER PYRAMID SCHEME VIDEO EVIDENCE

358
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,720
<i>Today, police raided and arrested</i>

359
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:25,000
<i>the M Power pyramid scheme network</i>
<i>run by Yollada Arayasai,</i>

360
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:27,360
<i>also known as Hi-So Mam.</i>

361
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:29,840
<i>She had been recruiting members</i>
<i>for over five years</i>

362
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:34,200
<i>until the scheme was exposed</i>
<i>by a mysterious figure known as Admin.</i>

363
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:37,040
<i>Sources also report that Admin's team</i>

364
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:39,880
<i>hacked into the M Power accounts</i>

365
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:42,720
<i>and returned the funds to the victims</i>

366
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:46,320
<i>just before Yollada</i>
<i>could shut down the company and flee.</i>

367
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:47,880
<i>I don't know who Admin is,</i>

368
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:51,160
<i>but I'm so grateful.</i>

369
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:52,080
VICTIMS OF THE M POWER PYRAMID SCHEME

370
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:55,880
<i>If I'd been scammed out of my money,</i>
<i>I wouldn't have known what to do.</i>

371
00:29:56,800 --> 00:30:00,360
<i>It was the last substantial amount</i>
<i>of money I had left.</i>

372
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:04,000
<i>Thank you.</i>

373
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:06,600
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

374
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:10,640
<i>I truly mean it.</i>

375
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:19,400
If one day I had no other choice…

376
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:24,400
maybe I'd do what Gusjang did.

377
00:30:27,320 --> 00:30:28,720
I think I finally understand

378
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:33,720
why people still fall for pyramid schemes.

379
00:30:36,600 --> 00:30:37,640
There's nothing wrong

380
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:40,800
with people dreaming
of getting rich one day.

381
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:44,240
The thing is, we mustn't get greedy,

382
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:47,600
and we shouldn't fool ourselves

383
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:51,040
into thinking what we're doing is right.

384
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:09,400
-<i>Stop lying already!</i>
-<i>You're the liar!</i>

385
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:12,760
For the past 13 years,
while you were running in panic,

386
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:16,720
you didn't even know
Hong spent all the money herself.

387
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:22,520
13 YEARS AGO

388
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:26,200
Gao! Phayak!

389
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,120
Gao! Pha--

390
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,640
Hong, what happened?

391
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:34,320
Mam tried to kill me.

392
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:38,200
<i>Breaking news. Kamnan Chang,</i>
<i>a suspect in a pyramid scheme case,</i>

393
00:31:38,280 --> 00:31:41,200
<i>was recently found dead</i>
<i>in a roadside forest</i>

394
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:42,920
<i>near the Bang Pakong Bypass.</i>

395
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:45,200
<i>Police preliminarily suspect</i>

396
00:31:45,280 --> 00:31:49,560
<i>the perpetrators may have been the group</i>
<i>that helped him escape.</i>

397
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:53,240
<i>Police now have descriptions</i>
<i>of all three suspects</i>

398
00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:55,360
<i>and are in the process</i>
<i>of tracking them down.</i>

399
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:56,640
SUSPECTS IN AIDING KAMNAN CHANG'S ESCAPE

400
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:01,240
Where's the payment we got
from Kamnan Chang?

401
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:02,240
Here.

402
00:32:08,080 --> 00:32:09,680
Take this money and split it up.

403
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:12,560
I've got some more
from what I managed to steal.

404
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:18,920
Now we need to split up and go on the run.

405
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,640
How long do we have to keep running?

406
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:21,840
I don't know.

407
00:32:22,360 --> 00:32:24,720
Let's just not contact each other for now.

408
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:25,920
Wait until things settle down.

409
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:27,400
Okay?

410
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:42,920
You're thinking about
what Mam said, right?

411
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:47,080
Hong.

412
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,960
Tell me what Mam said…

413
00:32:54,040 --> 00:32:55,160
It's not true, right?

414
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:57,320
So I don't have to worry.

415
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:01,200
Hong, tell me.

416
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,880
You guys.

417
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:15,240
What would you say

418
00:33:20,560 --> 00:33:22,080
if I told you…

419
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:28,000
that what Mam said…

420
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:44,240
is true?

421
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:53,000
You guys, can you forgive me?

422
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:54,960
Please.

423
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,000
Hong, why did you lie to me?

424
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,080
Hey.

425
00:34:03,160 --> 00:34:07,080
I know that back then,
I really was terrible. Can you forgive me?

426
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,280
What about now, Hong?

427
00:34:12,080 --> 00:34:13,880
With everything you did to us,

428
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:15,880
now we don't know

429
00:34:15,960 --> 00:34:17,600
what was real

430
00:34:18,880 --> 00:34:20,880
and what was a lie.

431
00:34:43,679 --> 00:34:45,080
-Another bottle already?
-Yeah.

432
00:34:45,159 --> 00:34:46,159
Isn't that too much?

433
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:57,520
THREE DAYS LATER

434
00:35:14,040 --> 00:35:15,520
Come down from there.

435
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:19,120
-Whoa, take it easy!
-Hey, I'm okay!

436
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:20,880
Step down, sis.

437
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,840
Come down slowly.

438
00:35:22,920 --> 00:35:25,760
If you're gonna dance like that,
there's plenty of space down here.

439
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:28,200
You're drinking way too much.
Come to my place if you're going hard.

440
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:30,320
You already got a new place?

441
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,960
Then let's celebrate

442
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:35,920
the grand opening
of the new Cocoa Cafe branch!

443
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,080
Cheers!

444
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:39,720
Come on, drink!

445
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,040
-Quick!
-Okay, here!

446
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:42,720
-Cheers!
-Alright.

447
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:44,560
Hey!

448
00:35:44,640 --> 00:35:46,040
You finished the whole bottle?

449
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:49,920
Amazing! I love it!

450
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:52,560
-Whoa! That's enough. Relax!
-Sis, stop!

451
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:54,280
No rush, sis.

452
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,000
I'm not in a hurry. Look.

453
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:58,000
But I'm in a hurry.

454
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:02,560
Is she sad or not?

455
00:36:03,760 --> 00:36:05,600
-I really can't tell.
-Dance with me!

456
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,440
-Dancing alone isn't any fun.
-Of course she's sad.

457
00:36:08,520 --> 00:36:10,240
She's masking it
by pretending to have fun.

458
00:36:10,320 --> 00:36:11,840
I can't dance. I don't know how.

459
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:17,640
-Sis, hang in there!
-Whoa!

460
00:36:17,720 --> 00:36:19,160
Hang in there!

461
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:22,200
I'm okay, really.

462
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,040
Wait, you already swallowed it?

463
00:36:25,560 --> 00:36:28,960
-Hey!
-Wait! Where are you going?

464
00:36:29,040 --> 00:36:31,600
To the bathroom. Just a sec.

465
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:33,800
What's wrong with you?

466
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:36,920
Wait a bit, then I'll be back. Okay?

467
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,520
-Don't go anywhere.
-Walk carefully!

468
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:39,640
Yeah!

469
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:51,120
<i>Hong, tell me what Mam said…</i>

470
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:54,440
<i>It's not true, right?</i>
<i>So I don't have to worry.</i>

471
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,000
<i>Hong, tell me.</i>

472
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,000
What would you say

473
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:03,360
if I told you that what Mam said…

474
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,960
is true?

475
00:37:07,160 --> 00:37:11,120
I know that back then,
I really was terrible. Can you forgive me?

476
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:12,320
What about now, Hong?

477
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:15,160
With everything you did to us,

478
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:17,160
now we don't know

479
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:18,880
what was real

480
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:21,080
and what was a lie.

481
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:49,360
Sis.

482
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:55,000
Risa, what are you doing here?

483
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:57,480
Hey, I'm partying with the guys.

484
00:37:57,560 --> 00:37:58,680
Come have a drink.

485
00:37:58,760 --> 00:37:59,880
Sis.

486
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:01,880
Are you okay?

487
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:04,960
I'm fine.

488
00:38:05,040 --> 00:38:06,840
Nothing's wrong. Hey.

489
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,440
Did I really look that drunk?

490
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:10,400
-Let's go!
-Sis.

491
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:13,800
You know that's not
what I'm talking about.

492
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:19,760
Sis.

493
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:22,560
Can I ask you something?

494
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:26,480
If you really took
the ten million back then,

495
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:32,080
why are you doing all this now?

496
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:40,520
You know,

497
00:38:41,400 --> 00:38:44,880
the ten million I got,
I spent it all within a few years.

498
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:47,360
What did you spend it on?

499
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,280
That's a lot of money.

500
00:38:50,640 --> 00:38:51,720
Were you gambling?

501
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:59,120
Back then, I had just found out…

502
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:03,200
I had cancer.

503
00:39:16,640 --> 00:39:17,800
Why so glum?

504
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,720
I don't know.

505
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:34,240
So what are we gonna do now?

506
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:38,080
I don't know.

507
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:40,760
Where are we driving to?

508
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:43,120
Don't know.

509
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:47,960
Damn it. Why don't we pull over
and figure it out?

510
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:51,000
Driving around like this is wasting gas.

511
00:39:51,080 --> 00:39:54,400
Why are you complaining? I just want
to drive us as far away as possible.

512
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,200
<i>I spent ten million</i>

513
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:09,800
chasing happiness,
grabbing everything I could

514
00:40:10,640 --> 00:40:12,280
before I died.

515
00:40:15,160 --> 00:40:16,440
But in the end,

516
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:19,480
I realized

517
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:22,600
it wasn't the happiness I wanted.

518
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:27,480
The real happiness I wanted

519
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:31,400
was those two old men.

520
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:00,960
-Gao.
-Huh?

521
00:41:03,520 --> 00:41:04,960
Want to go on a trip abroad?

522
00:41:09,160 --> 00:41:10,440
That could be nice.

523
00:41:23,200 --> 00:41:28,800
INMATE VISITATION HOURS

524
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:45,280
Mr. Louis!

525
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:47,080
Mr. Louis!

526
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:51,160
Never thought you'd slip up.

527
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:54,120
Don't worry, Mr. Louis.

528
00:41:54,200 --> 00:41:56,240
I'll handle this myself.

529
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:58,640
I won't get you involved.

530
00:42:00,640 --> 00:42:03,560
I think you've caused
enough trouble already.

531
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:12,360
Now tell me, who are they?

532
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:16,880
I remember all their faces.
I'm ready to tell you everything.

533
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:19,520
But you have to help me get out, okay?

534
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:21,040
I can help you.

535
00:42:21,640 --> 00:42:26,280
But it depends on how much
you can help me in return.

536
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,840
There are six of them.

537
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:31,160
Check the CCTV footage
behind the seminar room

538
00:42:31,240 --> 00:42:32,520
and in front of my condo.

539
00:42:32,600 --> 00:42:34,320
You'll see all their faces.

540
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:49,840
STAND WITHIN THE DESIGNATED AREA
NO TALKING

541
00:42:50,680 --> 00:42:53,680
Are you sure there are only six of them?

542
00:42:56,120 --> 00:42:58,960
Yes, that's all of them.

543
00:43:03,360 --> 00:43:06,160
Mr. Louis! You're not going to help me?

544
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:08,240
I thought you said you'd get me out!

545
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:13,320
When did I ever say that?

546
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:17,720
If you betray me,

547
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:19,640
I'll tell everything.

548
00:43:19,720 --> 00:43:22,240
If I go to prison,
everyone goes down with me.

549
00:43:22,320 --> 00:43:24,240
I'll tell the police everything

550
00:43:24,320 --> 00:43:25,880
and bring all of you down with me!

551
00:43:32,640 --> 00:43:34,440
But I believe you won't tell.

552
00:43:35,760 --> 00:43:37,080
Do you know why?

553
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:43,000
Because the dead can't talk.

554
00:43:51,040 --> 00:43:51,920
Step inside.

555
00:44:42,600 --> 00:44:44,400
Help! Somebody, help me!

556
00:44:44,480 --> 00:44:46,160
Help me!

557
00:44:50,840 --> 00:44:52,720
No! Don't!

558
00:44:54,720 --> 00:44:58,640
Help! Somebody, help me!

559
00:44:58,720 --> 00:45:01,240
Help! Somebody, help me!

560
00:45:02,520 --> 00:45:05,000
Okay, easy.

561
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:08,040
Put her down gently.

562
00:45:08,920 --> 00:45:11,360
She's drunk and thrashing around.
How gentle do you want me to be?

563
00:45:11,440 --> 00:45:13,440
You're a big guy.
That's all the strength you've got?

564
00:45:14,480 --> 00:45:15,520
Why don't you help her yourself?

565
00:45:15,600 --> 00:45:16,920
Step aside.

566
00:45:20,880 --> 00:45:21,960
Where is this place?

567
00:45:22,040 --> 00:45:24,200
It's my new place, sis.

568
00:45:25,320 --> 00:45:26,800
-Your new place?
-Yes.

569
00:45:28,320 --> 00:45:29,880
Great! Alright!

570
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:31,040
Bring me another beer!

571
00:45:31,120 --> 00:45:32,000
Come on!

572
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:33,240
-Hey!
-Hold on!

573
00:45:33,320 --> 00:45:34,920
-Sis!
-Watch out!

574
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:38,520
That's enough drinking. Just go to bed.

575
00:45:38,600 --> 00:45:40,120
Chen, is there a place to sleep here?

576
00:45:40,200 --> 00:45:41,840
Yeah, my room's in the back.

577
00:45:41,920 --> 00:45:43,280
Let's lay her down there.

578
00:45:43,360 --> 00:45:44,680
-Okay.
-Let's do that.

579
00:45:44,760 --> 00:45:45,600
Come on, sis.

580
00:45:47,560 --> 00:45:49,480
-See?
-Sis.

581
00:45:51,040 --> 00:45:53,280
What, can't do it?

582
00:45:53,360 --> 00:45:55,920
Now you know how heavy
a drunk person can be.

583
00:45:57,120 --> 00:45:58,000
Come on, sis.

584
00:45:58,680 --> 00:46:00,520
Hey. If you can't do it, step back.

585
00:46:06,520 --> 00:46:08,920
And next time, don't talk back.

586
00:46:09,680 --> 00:46:12,000
Whoa, sis.

587
00:46:12,880 --> 00:46:14,240
Come on, sis. Excuse me.

588
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:18,080
Whoa, sis!

589
00:46:18,160 --> 00:46:19,680
-Hey, careful!
-Sis!

590
00:46:20,280 --> 00:46:21,320
-This way!
-Whoa!

591
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:23,440
We got this!

592
00:46:23,520 --> 00:46:26,120
Get her inside. Go!

593
00:46:31,640 --> 00:46:32,560
Hey, Ris.

594
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:37,080
Why do you seem so worried
about Hong lately?

595
00:46:43,800 --> 00:46:44,840
She has cancer.

596
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:48,560
Cancer?

597
00:46:48,640 --> 00:46:49,720
Keep it down.

598
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:52,760
How'd you find out? Did she tell you?

599
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:58,920
That's also why she took

600
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:01,320
Gao and Phayak's money back then.

601
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:04,200
Whoa, what are we gonna do?

602
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:09,600
The gang's already falling apart,
and now Hong's like this.

603
00:47:10,480 --> 00:47:13,040
I don't think we can keep doing this.

604
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:17,920
You know, maybe if Admin finds out,

605
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:20,240
he won't assign us any more jobs.

606
00:47:22,320 --> 00:47:23,720
That might not be so bad.

607
00:47:24,840 --> 00:47:26,440
I don't want to do
this kind of work anymore.

608
00:47:29,800 --> 00:47:31,200
What's going on?

609
00:47:31,280 --> 00:47:32,360
Well…

610
00:47:33,760 --> 00:47:37,000
Just a few more jobs,
and I can pay off my dad's debt.

611
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:42,240
I'll finally be free.

612
00:47:43,240 --> 00:47:44,200
Really?

613
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:48,080
What will you do next? Go back to school?

614
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:07,000
Don't you have anything you want to do?

615
00:48:07,960 --> 00:48:10,880
Like a dream or something?

616
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:21,080
I don't know. Besides my dad,

617
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:24,240
I've never really thought
about anything else.

618
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:42,160
RUAMKATANYU FOUNDATION

619
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:48,040
INMATE VISITATION HOURS

620
00:48:50,760 --> 00:48:51,640
Wait.

621
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:06,240
RUANGRIT CHOKANUN

622
00:49:06,320 --> 00:49:08,480
Are you sure this was suicide?

623
00:49:08,560 --> 00:49:11,320
Yes. She used a towel,
tore it into strips, and hanged herself.

624
00:49:19,040 --> 00:49:19,880
Alright.

625
00:49:27,400 --> 00:49:29,640
I want the full list of visitor names.

626
00:49:31,200 --> 00:49:33,480
Yes, sir. I'll get it for you.

627
00:49:56,800 --> 00:49:59,520
What now ? You said
you wouldn't mess with us anymore.

628
00:49:59,600 --> 00:50:01,000
Mess with you?

629
00:50:01,080 --> 00:50:02,760
I just came to return the money.

630
00:50:02,840 --> 00:50:04,240
What's so funny?

631
00:50:04,320 --> 00:50:05,840
Your husband just paid off the debt.

632
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:08,160
On top of that, he completely wrecked us.

633
00:50:08,840 --> 00:50:10,880
-My husband?
-Yep.

634
00:50:10,960 --> 00:50:13,800
Long story short, your husband
came and cleared the debt.

635
00:50:13,880 --> 00:50:15,240
We're done.

636
00:50:15,320 --> 00:50:17,080
And I promised him

637
00:50:17,160 --> 00:50:19,440
I wouldn't bother you again. Okay?

638
00:50:19,520 --> 00:50:22,280
Husband? Which one?

639
00:50:22,360 --> 00:50:23,440
You have more than one?

640
00:50:24,360 --> 00:50:26,080
What does he look like?

641
00:50:26,160 --> 00:50:29,480
Well, he's tall and lanky,

642
00:50:29,560 --> 00:50:31,160
a bit of a troublemaker.

643
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:34,440
He brought his beefy friends.
They completely trashed us.

644
00:50:35,480 --> 00:50:38,200
33 MINUTES EARLIER

645
00:50:39,080 --> 00:50:39,960
She borrowed money.

646
00:50:40,040 --> 00:50:42,160
But why beat her up?

647
00:50:44,280 --> 00:50:45,480
Why did you do that?

648
00:50:45,560 --> 00:50:46,720
Hold on!

649
00:50:48,280 --> 00:50:51,120
I give up, sir.
Just tell me what you want.

650
00:50:51,200 --> 00:50:53,120
I've paid off

651
00:50:53,640 --> 00:50:54,960
all the debt she owed you.

652
00:50:56,360 --> 00:50:59,600
But my boss said
he's raising Arisa's interest rate

653
00:50:59,680 --> 00:51:01,880
from 20% to 30%.

654
00:51:04,840 --> 00:51:06,120
Thirty percent?

655
00:51:06,760 --> 00:51:09,280
That means if you borrow 100,

656
00:51:09,360 --> 00:51:10,600
the interest is 30.

657
00:51:10,680 --> 00:51:12,360
If you borrow a million,

658
00:51:12,440 --> 00:51:14,440
you'd owe 300,000 in interest?

659
00:51:14,520 --> 00:51:15,520
Yes.

660
00:51:16,720 --> 00:51:18,200
That's outrageous!

661
00:51:18,280 --> 00:51:19,080
I beg you.

662
00:51:19,160 --> 00:51:21,280
-Begging, huh?
-Enough, Chen.

663
00:51:28,880 --> 00:51:30,240
Another 1.8 million, right?

664
00:51:30,320 --> 00:51:31,480
Yes.

665
00:51:32,800 --> 00:51:35,280
Sure. Let's settle this.

666
00:51:36,440 --> 00:51:39,720
But don't you dare
get involved with her again.

667
00:51:40,240 --> 00:51:41,880
Or I'll kill you.

668
00:51:41,960 --> 00:51:44,600
Yes, sir. I promise.

669
00:51:45,840 --> 00:51:48,320
Did he tell you why he paid off my debt?

670
00:51:49,200 --> 00:51:52,120
How would I know? Go ask your husband.

671
00:51:52,200 --> 00:51:53,920
He's not my husband.

672
00:51:58,640 --> 00:52:01,600
RISA

673
00:52:06,080 --> 00:52:07,160
Why aren't you picking up?

674
00:52:12,920 --> 00:52:14,120
Come on, man.

675
00:52:21,840 --> 00:52:22,920
What's up?

676
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:24,640
Why did you pay off my debt?

677
00:52:26,680 --> 00:52:29,520
Are you crazy?
Why would I pay off your debt?

678
00:52:29,600 --> 00:52:32,360
Don't lie. That tall, lanky guy

679
00:52:32,440 --> 00:52:35,200
<i>with the beefy friend,</i>
<i>that's obviously you and Chen.</i>

680
00:52:35,280 --> 00:52:38,240
Tell me. Why did you pay off my debt?

681
00:52:38,320 --> 00:52:42,120
Well, I had some extra money
and didn't know what to do with it.

682
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:43,840
So I helped you.

683
00:52:43,920 --> 00:52:45,360
But why help me?

684
00:52:46,280 --> 00:52:47,200
I guess I like you.

685
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:51,400
Why can't you just tell me the truth?

686
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:53,560
What do you really want from me?

687
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:56,040
Why do you keep asking?

688
00:52:56,120 --> 00:52:58,280
I paid off your debt.
Isn't that a good thing?

689
00:52:58,360 --> 00:53:00,560
That's it. I don't have time to talk.

690
00:53:00,640 --> 00:53:01,600
Hey.

691
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:09,880
Koh.

692
00:53:10,400 --> 00:53:13,400
Why didn't you just tell her the truth
that you know her dad?

693
00:53:13,480 --> 00:53:15,360
What do you want me to say?

694
00:53:15,440 --> 00:53:16,960
"Hello, Risa.

695
00:53:17,040 --> 00:53:20,000
Sorry I had a part
in your dad's disappearance,

696
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:22,720
forcing you to scramble for money
to pay off his debt

697
00:53:22,800 --> 00:53:24,560
and ruining your life."

698
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:26,440
You want me to say that?

699
00:53:26,960 --> 00:53:27,960
Huh?

700
00:53:30,720 --> 00:53:32,040
You're right.

701
00:53:32,560 --> 00:53:36,400
At least what you did
counts as taking responsibility.

702
00:53:38,720 --> 00:53:42,840
That's why I wanted to know
whether Aek is still alive.

703
00:53:47,360 --> 00:53:49,960
Koh, can you tell me

704
00:53:50,600 --> 00:53:53,160
what really happened between you and Aek?

705
00:54:00,360 --> 00:54:03,240
FIVE YEARS AGO

706
00:54:07,240 --> 00:54:09,160
I have to take you to talk to him.

707
00:54:11,280 --> 00:54:13,320
He's got people out
looking for you everywhere.

708
00:54:13,400 --> 00:54:14,880
There's no way you'll get away.

709
00:54:14,960 --> 00:54:17,520
But if I go back with you,
I'm dead either way.

710
00:54:19,600 --> 00:54:20,880
Just let me go.

711
00:54:21,520 --> 00:54:23,760
I don't think you have a choice.

712
00:54:25,960 --> 00:54:28,360
He promised me he wouldn't hurt you.

713
00:54:30,320 --> 00:54:32,440
Go back and work it out with him.

714
00:54:32,520 --> 00:54:34,000
That's better than running off to die.

715
00:54:34,880 --> 00:54:36,000
I'm begging you.

716
00:55:06,040 --> 00:55:07,720
Why do we have to talk here?

717
00:55:10,600 --> 00:55:11,640
Trust me.

718
00:55:11,720 --> 00:55:14,920
As long as I'm here, no one can touch you.

719
00:55:46,280 --> 00:55:47,560
Why are you alone?

720
00:55:48,240 --> 00:55:50,000
Where are the people
who were supposed to help Aek?

721
00:55:51,800 --> 00:55:53,080
They're coming.

722
00:55:53,840 --> 00:55:54,800
Go wait inside.

723
00:55:58,720 --> 00:55:59,560
I'm not going in.

724
00:56:01,520 --> 00:56:03,880
He told you to go in, so go.

725
00:56:03,960 --> 00:56:06,000
I want you to deal with these guys.

726
00:56:06,080 --> 00:56:08,600
<i>They're the ones</i>
<i>who messed with Kluay and Mam.</i>

727
00:56:08,680 --> 00:56:10,040
Where's Aek now?

728
00:56:10,120 --> 00:56:11,840
I heard Mr. Louis captured him.

729
00:56:11,920 --> 00:56:13,480
And where can I find Louis?

730
00:56:13,560 --> 00:56:15,520
<i>The Hyena Group operates in Poipet.</i>

731
00:56:15,600 --> 00:56:17,760
<i>So Risa was tricked?</i>

732
00:56:17,840 --> 00:56:19,720
<i>Is this about Koh going to Cambodia?</i>

733
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:22,560
What do you know? Tell me everything now!

734
00:56:22,640 --> 00:56:25,760
<i>No one here</i>
<i>is allowed to contact outsiders.</i>

735
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:28,160
<i>Everyone gets a salary of 25,000.</i>

736
00:56:28,240 --> 00:56:31,600
<i>If anyone earns more than 200,000 a month,</i>
<i>there's a commission bonus.</i>

737
00:56:31,680 --> 00:56:34,240
So what's the job?

738
00:56:35,600 --> 00:56:39,560
Risa's in Poipet?
You guys stay back. I'll handle it.

739
00:56:39,640 --> 00:56:40,960
Risa's my dear friend.

740
00:56:41,800 --> 00:56:43,920
<i>If you expect me</i>
<i>to just stand by, I can't.</i>

741
00:57:31,520 --> 00:57:35,320
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
